_before_chunking.await?);","         builder = builder","             .chunking_config(","                 Vc::<EcmascriptChunkType>::default().to_resolved().await?,","                 ChunkingConfig {","                     // Server chunks are loaded with require(), not fetched over the network.","-                    min_chunk_size: chunking_min_chunk_size.unwrap_or(4_000),","+                    min_chunk_size: chunking_min_chunk_size.unwrap_or_else(|| defaults.size(4_000)),","                     max_chunk_count_per_group: 0,","-                    max_merge_chunk_size: chunking_max_merge_chunk_size.unwrap_or(100_000),","-                    request_cost: Some(10_000),","+                    max_merge_chunk_size: chunking_max_merge_chunk_size","+                        .unwrap_or_else(|| defaults.size(100_000)),","+                    request_cost: Some(defaults.request_cost(10_000)),","                     ..Default::default()","                 },","             )"],"additions":6,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/01-app/03-api-reference/05-config/01-next-config-js/turbopackChunking.mdx","lines":["@@ -122,6 +122,13 @@ When merging chunks, the trade-off being made is an improvement to performance o"," loads at the cost of navigation performance. This is because each additional network request"," being made is costly, however, smaller chunks are more likely to be re-usable across pages."," ","+> **Good to know**: The size thresholds depend on the experimental","+> `experimental.turbopackMinifyBeforeChunking` option. When it is enabled (and minification is on),","+> Turbopack minifies each module before chunking and measures sizes in bytes of minified code","+> instead. The default thresholds and `requestCost`, including the server chunk thresholds below,","+> are then scaled down to 40% of the values listed here. Values you set explicitly are used as-is,","+> so you may need to lower them when enabling the option.","+"," ## Server Chunks"," "," The size thresholds above only apply to client-side JavaScript. Server-side JavaScript for the"],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/next/src/server/config-shared.ts","lines":["@@ -904,6 +904,7 @@ export interface ExperimentalConfig {","   /**","    * Minify each module separately instead of each finished chunk, so minification runs in","    * parallel and is cached per module. The trade-off is slightly worse compression.","+   * Chunking then sizes modules by their minified code, see `turbopackChunking`.","    * Defaults to false. Only applies to production builds.","    */","   turbopackMinifyBeforeChunking?: boolean","@@ -918,6 +919,10 @@ export interface ExperimentalConfig {","   /**","    * (`next --turbopack` only) These options change the assumptions Turbopack makes when","    * making chunk merging decisions and the raw size thresholds it uses.","+   *","+   * Sizes are measured on unminified code, or on minified code when","+   * `turbopackMinifyBeforeChunking` applies. In that case the default sizes and request cost","+   * below are scaled down to match; values set here are used as-is.","    */","   turbopackChunking?: {","     /**"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"turbopack/crates/turbopack-core/src/chunk/chunking/mod.rs","lines":["@@ -32,6 +32,8 @@ mod dev;"," mod production;"," mod style_production;"," ","+pub use production::DEFAULT_ESTIMATED_REQUEST_COST_BYTES;","+"," #[turbo_tasks::value]"," struct ChunkItemsWithInfo {","     #[allow(clippy::type_complexity)]"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"turbopack/crates/turbopack-core/src/chunk/chunking/production.rs","lines":["@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ use crate::{"," };"," "," /// Default estimated cost of an additional request, in bytes (200 KB).","-const DEFAULT_ESTIMATED_REQUEST_COST_BYTES: u64 = 200_000;","+pub const DEFAULT_ESTIMATED_REQUEST_COST_BYTES: u64 = 200_000;"," "," /// Probability that a navigation stays within a cluster."," cons